(test
 (name test_ohcamel)
 ; test_example_book parses the committed example book, which the image bakes in
 ; as its fallback and deploy.sh copies onto a fresh host. test_contract's oracle
 ; reads interface/examples/*.json against expected.json (ruling 6's
 ; cross-language check), so its glob is a dep the same way.
 ; research/config/friction_v1.yaml: the one-cost-configuration test holds the
 ; example book's half-spreads to it. desk/ and bin/: the one-submit-site test
 ; reads every source file there for a mention of the wire module, which only
 ; the order manager's one submit may make.
 ; lib/factor_model.ml: the shared-minimum case reads its one definition line,
 ; because whether that line reads Risk_metrics' constant or a literal 120 of
 ; its own is invisible at runtime -- both are 120.
 ; ../bin/main.exe: test_example_book runs the binary for the modes whose whole
 ; contract is an exit code -- check-book exits 0 or 1 and deploy.sh reads
 ; nothing else of it, and a mistyped port exits 2 with the usage. Both are
 ; decided in the dispatcher, before block_on_async_exn, so the spawned process
 ; opens no socket and starts no scheduler: this suite's promise still holds.
 ; The child is forked and waited on against a deadline (unix, below), so a
 ; regression that turned one of those into a server would be killed and
 ; reported, not sat on.
 (deps
  ../book.example.sexp
  ../bin/main.exe
  ../lib/factor_model.ml
  ../research/config/friction_v1.yaml
  (glob_files ../desk/*.ml)
  (glob_files ../desk/*.mli)
  (glob_files ../bin/*.ml)
  (glob_files ../interface/examples/*.json))
 ; qcheck-core supplies the generators and qcheck-alcotest turns a property into
 ; an ordinary alcotest case, which is what keeps the example-based and
 ; property-based suites in ONE runner. Two runners would mean two things to
 ; remember to run, and the one that gets forgotten is the one that fails.
 ; test/desk_async is a second runner, for the cases that need the scheduler --
 ; this suite's own promise is that it never starts one. `dune runtest` runs
 ; both, so forgetting one still isn't possible; it is two things to read, not
 ; two things to remember to run.
 ; yojson: the reproducibility pins parse web/quoted.json (Quoted.json).
 ; ohcamel_desk and sqlite3: the desk's suites, and the journal test that writes a file with a schema version this build refuses.
 ; unix: test_example_book forks the binary and bounds it by the wall clock.
 (libraries
  ohcamel
  ohcamel_desk
  sqlite3
  alcotest
  qcheck-core
  qcheck-alcotest
  yojson
  unix))
